# Sweep AI cost control

- While a sweep arm or stage is running, do not launch recurring AI status checks or
  repeatedly analyze partial results. Use local process/log inspection only when the
  user explicitly asks for current status.
- Analyze a sweep once, after its `sweep finished` marker and compact completion request
  exist under `reports/ai/requests/`.
- For that analysis, use only the corresponding `reports/ai/*_summary.json`, generated
  from `reports/experiments.jsonl`.
- Never attach or ingest `reports/trades.csv`, `reports/logs/`, raw arm logs, or the full
  `experiments.jsonl` into an AI prompt.
- A request filename includes a result fingerprint. Treat an existing request with the
  same fingerprint as already requested; do not request another analysis.
